<header><p class="st-kicker">princely state · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Dhurwai State</h1><p class="st-meta">1800 CE – 1950 CE (approx.) · capital Dhurwai</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A tiny Bundela chiefship of the Bundelkhand Agency in central India.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Dhurwai was recognised by the British as a separate holding in the early 19th century, one of the small <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> estates confirmed after the British gained control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>It consisted of a few villages under a hereditary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundela">Bundela</a> chief. Little else is recorded of its history.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After independence Dhurwai was merged into <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/vindhya-pradesh">Vindhya Pradesh</a> with the other <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bundelkhand">Bundelkhand</a> states and absorbed by 1950.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/dhurwai-state.jpg" alt="Dhurwai State" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Xufanc · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Dhurwai_state.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1800 CE – 1950 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>princely state</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dhurwai</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bundeli</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Dhurwai</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1875&amp;focus=dhurwai-state" aria-label="Dhurwai State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6774 1246 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Dhurwai State lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7094 1502L7364 1601M7094 1502L7364 1602M7094 1502L7160 1530"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7364 1601h0M7364 1602h0M7160 1530h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7094 1502h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7094 1502h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1875&amp;focus=dhurwai-state">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
